  "question": {
    "text": "A Carnot engine takes $3 \\times 10^6 \\mathrm{cal}$. of heat from a reservoir at $627^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, and gives it to a sink at $27^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. The work done by the engine is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "zqQYb",
      "text": "\n$4.2 \\times 10^6 \\mathrm{~J}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "L9C8G",
      "text": "\n$8.4 \\times 10^6 \\mathrm{~J}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "U4Ouw",
      "text": "\n$16.8 \\times 10^6 \\mathrm{~J}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ELKZR",
      "text": "\nZero",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\eta=\\frac{(627+273)-(273+27)}{627+273}$\n$=\\frac{900-300}{900}=\\frac{600}{900}=\\frac{2}{3}$\nwork $=(\\eta) \\times$ Heat\n$=\\frac{2}{3} \\times 3 \\times 10^6 \\times 4.2 \\mathrm{~J}=8.4 \\times 10^6 \\mathrm{~J}$",
    "image": null
  },
